---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kids' pottery classes"
	description="Run kids' pottery classes alongside your adult studio: parent sign-up with guardian consent, kids' class packs, self-filling waitlists and pickup texts to parents."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Kids' classes</p>
				<h1>Kids' classes without the clipboard.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Saturday wheel club, after-school hand-building, summer camp week. Kilnbook books the kids,
					collects the parent paperwork and tells families when the pinch pots are ready, while the
					rest of your studio keeps running.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/class-pack.svg"
				alt="A six-class pack card with three classes used and a waitlist card for a Tuesday evening session"
				width="480"
				height="320"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Kids' classes on the same calendar as everything else</h2>
		<p>
			Kids' sessions sit on the same schedule as your adult courses, open studio and
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">wheel reservations</a>. Block the six wheels a kids' class uses
			for its time slot and members simply can't book them for that hour. No double-booked wheels, and
			no surprise when twelve eight-year-olds walk in on a member's Saturday throw.
		</p>

		<h2>Parents sign up, and the consent comes with it</h2>
		<p>
			Parents book from your class page on their phone and add each child by name and age. Add your
			waiver or guardian consent form to the booking, and the seat isn't confirmed until a parent has
			agreed to it. Every child on the roster arrives with
			consent already given, so nobody is chasing paper at the door.
		</p>

		<h2>Sessions sized for kids</h2>
		<p>
			A kids' wheel session might be 45 minutes, not the two hours an adult course runs. Set the
			length per class, and sell kids' courses, drop-ins and class packs with their own prices,
			separate from adult packs. A parent who buys a 5-class kids' pack spends one credit per Saturday
			drop-in.
		</p>

		<h2>Rosters and waitlists that run themselves</h2>
		<p>
			Kids' classes fill fast, especially summer camp. When one is full, parents join the waitlist. If
			a family cancels, Kilnbook moves the next child on the waitlist into the open seat and updates
			the roster, without anyone at the front desk lifting a finger.
		</p>

		<h2>Every pinch pot gets home</h2>
		<p>
			Kids' work goes into the <a href="/features/firings">firing queue</a> like everyone else's, tagged
			with the child's name and class, so a shelf of small bowls stays sorted. Parents get a text when
			the bisque load is fired, and another when the glazed piece is ready for pickup.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">How it fits together</p>
			<h2>The features behind your kids' program</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Classes &amp; packs</h3>
					<p>
						Courses, drop-ins and class packs for kids and adults, with waitlists that fill seats on
						their own.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Wheel time</h3>
					<p>
						Members reserve wheels and tables in one-hour blocks around the times your kids' classes
						use them.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Kiln firings</h3>
					<p>
						Every piece is tracked from the bisque shelf to the pickup shelf, with texts when work is
						ready.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Make room for the kids.</h2>
			<p>Try Kilnbook free for 30 days. No card required.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
